Line 1: A file's name goes in quotes, like "grades.csv".
    Read file grades.csv.
              ^^^^^^^^^^
To read a table, write "read the table in "grades.csv" and call it grades".

Line 2: A file's name goes in quotes, like "best_months.csv".
    read best_months.csv and call it data
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
To read a table, write "read the table in "best_months.csv" and call it best months".

Line 6: A file's name goes in quotes, like "listings.xlsx".
    open listings.xlsx
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
EasyScript can't read Excel files yet. Save the sheet as a csv file in Excel ("Save As", then "CSV"), and read that.

Line 3: I don't know a sentence that starts with "open".
    open the file "guests.csv".
    ^^^^
To read a table, write "read the table in "guests.csv" and call it guests".

Line 4: I expected "file" or "the table in" here, but found the text "orders.csv".
    read "orders.csv"
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^
To read a table, write "read the table in "orders.csv" and call it orders".

Line 5: I don't know a sentence that starts with "load".
    load "notes.txt"
    ^^^^
